  | [.gitignore](https://github.com/isaackogan/TikTokLive/blob/master/.gitignore ".gitignore") | [.gitignore](https://github.com/isaackogan/TikTokLive/blob/master/.gitignore ".gitignore") | [fix(types): drop redundant inline annotations causing \[no-redef\]](https://github.com/isaackogan/TikTokLive/commit/d73d74fe1b691e1d913c5386c8404fc83ca6123f "fix(types): drop redundant inline annotations causing [no-redef]  mypy [no-redef] fires when a name is re-annotated mid-scope. Three patterns appeared across the codebase, all fixable by removing the second annotation and trusting mypy's flow analysis:  - Conditional narrowing: ``if uri is None: uri: str = ...`` re-declared   what the parameter already typed (ws_connect.py). - Param-shadow in route handlers: ``session_id: str = session_id or   cookies.get(...)`` re-annotated each function arg with a narrower type   (send_room_chat.py, fetch_signed_websocket.py). - Attribute re-declaration: ``self._room_id: int = ...`` after   ``self._room_id: Optional[int] = None`` in ``__init__``   (client.py, ws_client.py, fetch_video_data.py).  Other cleanups bundled in: - events/__init__.py: drop the dead try/except fallback for   proto_events. The codegen-bootstrap problem it guarded is gone now   that proto_events.py is committed and always present. - errors.py: rename the ``framed_message`` local in   ``format_sign_server_message`` so it stops shadowing the parameter. - ws_connect.py: collapse the parsed-tuple-then-list dance in   ``_convert_proxy`` by passing the parse_proxy_url result through   ``list(...)`` directly. - fetch_room_info.py: declare ``url`` and ``extra_params`` once before   the if/else, assign in branches; rename the inner narrowing to   ``resolved_room_id`` so it doesn't shadow the parameter.  Net mypy delta: 68 -> 47 errors (-21, including 4 cascades that were masking other types because of the redef).") | 5 months agoApr 29, 2026 |
