  ## Frequently Asked Questions
  
  ### Is there a public API for live stream data?
  
  There is no first-party public API specifically for live stream events. TikTool is an independent, third-party managed API service with 99.9% uptime that gives developers real-time access to chat, gifts, viewers, battles, and more. TikTool is not affiliated with or endorsed by any streaming platform.
  
  ### Is the TikTok LIVE API free?
  
  Yes. TikTool offers a free Sandbox tier with 3 concurrent WebSocket connections and 5,000 REST API requests per day. No credit card required. Paid plans start at $7/week (Basic) for 10,000 requests/day and 20 concurrent connections.
  
  ### What programming languages does the TikTok LIVE API support?
  
  TikTool works with any language. Official SDKs are available for Node.js (npm: @tiktool/live) and Python (pip: tiktok-live-api). The raw WebSocket API at wss://api.tik.tools works with Go, Rust, Java, C#, Ruby, PHP, Dart, Kotlin, Swift, and any language with WebSocket support.
  
  ### How is TikTool different from open-source live stream libraries?
  
  Open-source libraries require you to maintain connection infrastructure and break when the platform updates. TikTool is a managed API service - we handle all maintenance, challenge solving, and room authentication server-side. Your integration stays stable and production-ready.
  
  ### What data can I get from TikTok LIVE streams?
  
  Over 18 event types: chat messages, virtual gifts (with diamond values), likes, follows, shares, viewer counts, battle scores, pinned messages, stream status, and more. Plus unique AI-powered live captions for real-time speech-to-text transcription and translation.
  
  ### What is the latency?
  
  Sub-50 milliseconds. TikTool delivers events within 50ms of them occurring on TikTok. The managed WebSocket connection is optimized for low-latency real-time data delivery.
  
  ### Can I build a TikTok LIVE chat assistant?
  
  Yes. TikTool's real-time chat events include full user info, message text, emotes, and badges. Many developers build interactive chat assistants, moderation tools, command systems, and automated gift responses with TikTool.
  
  ### How many streams can I monitor simultaneously?
  
  Sandbox: 15 connections. Pro ($15/wk): 50. Ultra ($45/wk): 250. Agency ($119/wk): 250 + Live Gifter Firehose WS. Higher volumes are available on request.
  
  ### How does TikTool compare to Euler Stream?
  
  TikTool and Euler Stream are independent managed TikTok LIVE services with different feature focuses. Euler Stream is the signing backend used by the open-source tiktok-live-connector (Node.js) and TikTokLive (Python) libraries, maintained by the same team. TikTool runs its own independent signing infrastructure and adds features Euler does not currently offer - AI Live Captions and an agency intel layer. Both providers offer free tiers and paid plans; compare current pricing and quotas directly on each site.
  
  ### Is TikTool better than TikFinity for developers?
  
  TikFinity is a streaming tool for overlays and alerts - great for non-technical TikTok creators. TikTool is a developer API with WebSocket endpoints, SDKs, and REST APIs for building custom applications. If you need to build a custom chat assistant, analytics dashboard, or game integration, TikTool is the right choice. If you just want pre-built overlays without writing code, TikFinity may suit your needs.
  
  ### Can I use TikTok LIVE API for stream analytics?
  
  Yes. TikTool provides real-time viewer counts, engagement rates, gift revenue tracking, chat activity metrics, and battle scores. Many developers use our API to build custom analytics dashboards for streamers, agencies, and talent managers.
  
  ### Does the TikTok LIVE API work with OBS and Streamlabs?
  
  Yes. You can use TikTool's WebSocket API to build custom browser-source overlays for OBS, Streamlabs, and TikTok Live Studio. Display real-time chat, gift alerts, viewer counts, and battle scores directly on your stream.
  
